# "orbit off"; freeze also refused while spectating; the freeze line shows its limit; README rules exact;
# static_asserts tie the path's radius range to the orbit's. Apply this OR the draft, not both.
# Order: r102_camera-mode-1-2.py apply, then this. While this is applied, r102_camera-mode-1-2.py check
# reports "neither state" for mouse_camera.cpp/.h, bbport_overlay.cpp and README.md (this patch edits
# inside its blocks): that is expected; revert THIS first, then 1-2.
# usage: python -I -X utf8 r102_camera-mode-3-4.fixed.py check|apply|revert   (root: env R102_CAMERA_MODE_3_4_ROOT)
# Each edit replaces text found exactly once (the anchor) and refuses otherwise; revert replaces each
# new text (found exactly once) by its old text in reverse order, so patches applied after this one
# in other places of the same files stay. New files are written by apply and removed by revert (only
# while unchanged). Line ends: every file keeps its own (CRLF in the tree); new files get CRLF when the
# root's README.md has CRLF. Backups of every file touched go to <script>_backup next to the script.
